[Figure: A right triangle with legs a (vertical) and b (horizontal), and hypotenuse c. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

For the right triangle shown, a = 4 and b = 5. Which expression represents the value of c?
A. 4 + 5
B. \sqrt{(4)(5)}
C. \sqrt{4} + 5
D. \sqrt{4^2 + 5^2}

A right triangle has legs with lengths of 11 centimeters and 9 centimeters. What is the length of this triangle's hypotenuse, in centimeters?
A. \sqrt{40}
B. \sqrt{202}
C. 20
D. 202

[Figure: A right triangle with an angle x^\circ at the top left, hypotenuse 73, and horizontal leg 63. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

In the right triangle shown, what is the value of \sin x^\circ?
A. \frac{1}{73}
B. \frac{10}{73}
C. \frac{63}{73}
D. \frac{136}{73}

Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF, where angle A corresponds to angle D, and angles C and F are right angles. If \cos B = \frac{1}{22}, what is the value of \cos E?
A. \frac{1}{22}
B. \frac{1}{23}
C. \frac{21}{22}
D. \frac{22}{23}

[Figure: A right triangle with angle x^\circ at the top left, vertical leg 7, and horizontal leg 26. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

In the triangle shown, what is the value of \tan x^\circ?
A. \frac{1}{26}
B. \frac{19}{26}
C. \frac{26}{7}
D. \frac{33}{7}

[Figure: Right triangle ABC with the right angle at C. Vertex B is at top, vertex A at bottom right, vertex C at bottom left. Side BC = 35, hypotenuse AB = 171. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

In the right triangle shown, what is the value of \sin A?
A. \frac{1}{171}
B. \frac{35}{171}
C. \frac{171}{35}
D. 171

The length of a rectangle's diagonal is 5\sqrt{17}, and the length of the rectangle's shorter side is 5. What is the length of the rectangle's longer side?
A. \sqrt{17}
B. 20
C. 15\sqrt{2}
D. 400

[Figure: Triangle ABC with point D on AC such that BD is the altitude. Angle ABD = 30^\circ, angle DBC = 60^\circ. Side BC = 12.]

In \triangle ABC above, what is the length of \overline{AD}?
A. 4
B. 6
C. 6\sqrt{2}
D. 6\sqrt{3}

A right triangle has legs with lengths of 28 centimeters and 20 centimeters. What is the length of this triangle's hypotenuse, in centimeters?
A. 8\sqrt{6}
B. 4\sqrt{74}
C. 48
D. 1,184

[Figure: A right triangle with hypotenuse 21, vertical leg 6, and horizontal leg a. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

For the triangle shown, which expression represents the value of a?
A. \sqrt{21^2 - 6^2}
B. 21^2 - 6^2
C. \sqrt{21 - 6}
D. 21 - 6

[Figure: Right triangle ABC with right angle at C. Vertex B at top right, vertex A at bottom left, vertex C at bottom right. Hypotenuse AB = 42, horizontal leg AC = 41. Note: Figure not drawn to scale.]

What is the value of \cos A in the triangle shown?
A. \frac{42}{41}
B. \frac{41}{42}
C. \frac{1}{42}
D. \frac{1}{41}

[Figure: Right triangle ABC with right angle at C. Vertex B at top, vertex A at bottom left, vertex C at bottom right. Hypotenuse AB = 29, vertical leg BC = 20, horizontal leg AC = 21.]

In the figure above, what is the value of \tan(A)?
A. \frac{20}{29}
B. \frac{21}{29}
C. \frac{20}{21}
D. \frac{21}{20}

In a right triangle, the tangent of one of the two acute angles is \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}. What is the tangent of the other acute angle?
A. -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
B. -\frac{3}{\sqrt{3}}
C. \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
D. \frac{3}{\sqrt{3}}

A square is inscribed in a circle. The radius of the circle is \frac{20\sqrt{2}}{2} inches. What is the side length, in inches, of the square?
A. 20
B. \frac{20\sqrt{2}}{2}
C. 20\sqrt{2}
D. 40

Triangle ABC is similar to triangle DEF, where A corresponds to D and C corresponds to F. Angles C and F are right angles. If \tan(A) = \sqrt{3} and DF = 125, what is the length of \overline{DE}?
A. 125\frac{\sqrt{3}}{3}
B. 125\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}
C. 125\sqrt{3}
D. 250

